#{[{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046644} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507587} :activity/id #uuid "41eabed7-eb35-5f45-ae65-a1549a8e0311" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049896 :topic/id #uuid "1c8e94f0-f686-5ab0-b88e-99e6f26eaf54" :topic/math-academy-id 3232} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507538 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507441 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0692da6b-ac17-55ad-9bcd-1f26bdf2ad6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2s-5}{(s-2)(s-3)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506688}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506688} :answer-field/id #uuid "d0642696-6971-5290-bc2b-f5e549ec1a8d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507370}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "5aba7ba8-bc90-5a73-9994-754c33e2f759" :question/math-academy-id "q-332038" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+4{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{3s-8}{(s-2)(s-3)},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we find the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t)\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{-{x}_{1}(t)+4{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+2L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=-L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+4L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-3={X}_{1}(s)+2{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-2=-{X}_{1}(s)+4{X}_{2}(s)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$\n\nRewriting the system in standard form, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}(s-1){X}_{1}(s)-2{X}_{2}(s)=3 \\\\ {X}_{1}(s)+(s-4){X}_{2}(s)=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the second equation, we have \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=2-(s-4){X}_{2}(s).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(s-1)[2-(s-4){X}_{2}(s)]-2{X}_{2}(s) & =3 \\\\ 2(s-1)-[(s-1)(s-4)+2]{X}_{2}(s) & =3 \\\\ -({s}^{2}-5s+6){X}_{2}(s) & =3-2(s-1) \\\\ -(s-2)(s-3){X}_{2}(s) & =-2s+5 \\\\ {X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{2s-5}{(s-2)(s-3)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find ${X}_{1}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{X}_{1}(s) & =2-(s-4){X}_{2}(s) \\\\  & =2-(s-4)\\cdot \\frac{2s-5}{(s-2)(s-3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(s-2)(s-3)-(s-4)(2s-5)}{(s-2)(s-3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{3s-8}{(s-2)(s-3)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{3s-8}{(s-2)(s-3)},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{2s-5}{(s-2)(s-3)}.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "20ed4341-142c-5d21-8a9d-5dcc594bddbe" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507560}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507549 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507519 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "96a96d60-5df7-525f-b9d5-460b27317666" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{s-3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507005}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507005} :answer-field/id #uuid "7ea34c0d-6f70-52cb-8ac2-9e4d837fa8f2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507313} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b891e4e8-a932-5e13-8640-98de8fa2c1b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{-2s-2}{(s-3)(s-1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507085}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507085} :answer-field/id #uuid "b1cf17fd-da35-507f-b449-a0c201f4cbdd" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507354}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e1650579-5a44-5386-9786-86764c11f1fe" :question/math-academy-id "q-331915" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=3{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-2{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=$ {{field-1}},\n$\\,{X}_{2}(s)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we find the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{3{x}_{1}(t)\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{-2{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=3L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=-2L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-4=3{X}_{1}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)+2=-2{X}_{1}(s)+{X}_{2}(s)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$\n\nNow, solving the first equation for ${X}_{1}(s),$ we get\n\n$$\ns{X}_{1}(s)-4=3{X}_{1}(s)\\,⟹\\,{X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{4}{s-3}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this in the second equation and solving for ${X}_{2}(s),$ we have\n\n$$\ns{X}_{2}(s)+2=-2(\\frac{4}{s-3})+{X}_{2}(s)\\,⟹\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{-2s-2}{(s-1)(s-3)}.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "4f938b5a-9fc6-52bb-ada7-1b71f278f26f" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507538}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507560 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507472 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a25cd5e-273b-5e0e-9040-00a8c2d10252" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506774}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506774} :answer-field/id #uuid "4baf5e43-602f-5a2a-af70-6e70b13c11b5" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507283} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16629947-5e40-577a-9d59-2c4eb055b348" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506721}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506721} :answer-field/id #uuid "7225371b-bd06-5f60-a97e-ad353ead8edd" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507305} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25cc5a4e-ca9b-57bd-9bdf-37feb9b64059" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506763}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506763} :answer-field/id #uuid "9523a40b-2cb7-5f8d-a383-7ba5eb9b0d40" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507333} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cecdaf07-fce9-5488-9f84-191bfeae49d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507127}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507127} :answer-field/id #uuid "ebae569e-81df-5f8a-a1a7-dc127fd41a2e" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507385}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "a3c3395d-f560-5a1d-9156-22f49e61fe66" :question/math-academy-id "q-332290" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+4{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}=\\frac{2}{s-2},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}=\\frac{1}{s-2}-\\frac{4}{s-4}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,{e}^{2t}+\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,{e}^{4t}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-4}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{1}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{2}{s-2}\\} \\\\  & =2{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-2}\\} \\\\  & =2{e}^{2\\cdot t} \\\\  & =2{e}^{2t} \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{2}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-2}-\\frac{4}{s-4}\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-2}\\}-4{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-4}\\} \\\\  & ={e}^{2\\cdot t}-4{e}^{4\\cdot t} \\\\  & ={e}^{2t}-4{e}^{4t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{2t} \\\\ {e}^{2t}-4{e}^{4t}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]{e}^{4t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "8104dbdf-36d0-5a9c-af1e-91945fd05ed6"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507570 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507462 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "31a95984-f3ff-5d40-aa45-92f765a76484" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3s-1}{(s+1)(s-2)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506796}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506796} :answer-field/id #uuid "35230cec-1558-5848-ab5a-d11ccbfeb44d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507269} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e846976b-6bbf-5002-a11d-4c4ba08add2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{s+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507190}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507190} :answer-field/id #uuid "b6f7f1d9-3783-567e-8823-55b10da69ad9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507357}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "9a8a2b45-1f2b-5de6-b95b-a5731dcdb607" :question/math-academy-id "q-331914" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=4{x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=$ {{field-1}},\n$\\,{X}_{2}(s)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we find the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{-{x}_{1}(t)\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{4{x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=-L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=4L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+2L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)+1=-{X}_{1}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-3=4{X}_{1}(s)+2{X}_{2}(s)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$\n\nNow, solving the first equation for ${X}_{1}(s),$ we get\n\n$$\ns{X}_{1}(s)+1=-{X}_{1}(s)\\,⟹\\,{X}_{1}(s)=-\\frac{1}{s+1}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this in the second equation and solving for ${X}_{2}(s),$ we have\n\n$$\ns{X}_{2}(s)-3=4(-\\frac{1}{s+1})+2{X}_{2}(s)\\,⟹\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{3s-1}{(s+1)(s-2)}.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "b0b567e9-654d-55d5-b9dc-8fd5d056d374" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507549}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507587 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167161 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "96875261-1814-5e7b-b61f-3304d81295e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507004}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507004} :answer-field/id #uuid "b3dadf3b-7159-55f9-a626-90fba9eed477" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164010} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2fa1b31a-f357-5564-b7cd-7e75d306bc93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506793}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506793} :answer-field/id #uuid "c950654f-244e-5514-befa-91dd1f50705b" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164011} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ca18861d-726a-5a83-b401-6cdb30bef373" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507118}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507118} :answer-field/id #uuid "dbeeb397-fe1f-5065-8997-1a7a9ff96c66" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164012} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "94d2d8dc-c36f-51da-9b72-eac13162db91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507002}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507002} :answer-field/id #uuid "22f5e3fa-b810-513c-96f1-e73398a170ae" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164013}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "6b769427-838e-5978-9061-abde5d64f343" :question/math-academy-id "q-322289" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)-2{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}=\\frac{10}{s}-\\frac{1}{s-3},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}=\\frac{5}{s}+\\frac{1}{s-3}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,+\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,{e}^{3t}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-4}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{2}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{10}{s}-\\frac{1}{s-3}\\} \\\\  & =10{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}\\}-{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-3}\\} \\\\  & =10\\cdot 1-{e}^{3\\cdot t} \\\\  & =10-{e}^{3t} \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{2}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{5}{s}+\\frac{1}{s-3}\\} \\\\  & =5{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}\\}+{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-3}\\} \\\\  & =5\\cdot 1+{e}^{3\\cdot t} \\\\  & =5+{e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}10-{e}^{3t} \\\\ 5+{e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "e6ac8913-bf9c-5ca3-8750-bc65c8b2ddd7" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507570}}] :activity/title "Solving Homogeneous Systems of ODEs Using Laplace Transforms" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506666}]}
